OL,3,GNEWSAEyesore or icon - should city     
OL,4,Alandmark stay or go?                   
OL,6,FThe Yorkshire Post clock tower has been
OL,7,Fa Leeds landmark for as long as many   
OL,8,Fpeople in the city can remember.       
OL,10,F"I have just never known it not be     
OL,11,Fthere," says 56-year-old Jacquie       
OL,12,FRaistritk, who is the same age as the  
OL,13,Ftower which has overlooked Wellington  
OL,14,FStreet since 1970.                     
OL,16,F"It's a landmark, although it's fairly 
OL,17,Fugly."                                 
OL,19,FBut, whether you like it or loathe it, 
OL,20,Fthe clock and temperature gauge could  
OL,21,Fsoon be gone for good.                 
